%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f125b745d539af443b514f6298b234dc, type: 3}
  m_Name: WiseManPracticesLocalization_EN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  vignettes:
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 1657986904, guid: 3814edea3e5849f48ba217cf4bee6dd3, type: 3}
    text: "This is a very dangerous place\u2026  But once it was peaceful\u2026 The
      horrible looking creatures you saw were people once, like us. Then, they gave
      in into being unfair to others, they were made to believe they could have everything
      they wanted. They lost all humanity in them and now their soul is lost somewhere\u2026
      We call them Maligors"
    placement: 0
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 1251884205, guid: 3814edea3e5849f48ba217cf4bee6dd3, type: 3}
    text: "For the swamp to be safe again, everyone has to be treated with fairness,
      everyone deserves to find a safe place... We'll teach you what you need to
      know... to save them\u2026 to fight inequalities once and for all\u2026 Bring
      these poor souls here with us\u2026"
    placement: 0
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c0bde23d5e9b79448d39adc3cefb483, type: 3}
    text: When we meet someone for the first time, the first thing we do is explore
      who and how they are, if we have things in common, if we share hobbies or values...
      These are the foundations, the building blocks of a relationship. Individuals
      start sharing more personal details and testing the boundaries of their connection.
    placement: 1
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c0bde23d5e9b79448d39adc3cefb483, type: 3}
    text: There is always something in common with everyone, but you have to get
      closer to that person to discover it. The more you share, the more likely you
      are to become friends. And if you become friends, you will have established
      a bond with that person.
    placement: 1
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c0bde23d5e9b79448d39adc3cefb483, type: 3}
    text: "If all goes well, that bond can last a lifetime, and that\u2019s awesome!
      But there are always arguments or disagreements that need to be resolved."
    placement: 1
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c0bde23d5e9b79448d39adc3cefb483, type: 3}
    text: "Meeting people and bonding is awesome\u2026 But relationships can change,
      difficulties may arise and it is important to know how to navigate them to
      build successful and enduring connections."
    placement: 3
  - backgroundImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6c0bde23d5e9b79448d39adc3cefb483, type: 3}
    text: "Also, relationships can deteriorate. Sometimes people change, or life
      takes us on different paths\u2026 And then, friends or couples can feel more
      and more disconnected, more and more distant... Until the relationship ends.
      Even if saying goodbye may be painful, sometimes it's best to let someone go\u2026"
    placement: 3
  conflicts:
  - dialogues:
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: "Let me introduce you to Eve, she is a really good football player\u2026"
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    - characterName: Eve
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04816276ad4c8b64d80af5a19987b4b4, type: 3}
      text: Do you like football?
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: No
        responseFeedback: "Eve is a bit confused now, you\u2019ve been real, but
          maybe not so respectful or responsible\u2026 I think Eve no longer feels
          comfortable talking to you\u2026"
      - responseText: "No, but I\u2019m interested in your experience. Tell me more
          about you\u2026"
        responseFeedback: 
      - responseText: Yes, I like it a lot
        responseFeedback: "Eve feels good now because she notices your interest and
          is open to getting to know you too. You\u2019ve been real, responsible,
          responsive and respectful. Great!"
    - characterName: Eve
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04816276ad4c8b64d80af5a19987b4b4, type: 3}
      text: "Maybe we can launch a women\u2019s football club!"
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    requiresAllFeedback: 0
    isBranchingConflict: 0
  - dialogues:
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: "Imagine that you, Anna and your friends have been planning the opening
        of the women\u2019s football club for a long time, but at the last minute,
        it is not possible to go on with it ... In these examples, who do you think
        communicates more effectively?"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: One of them is criticizing the others for their opinion/attitude/behavior.
        responseFeedback: "They is being a bit aggressive, don\u2019t you think?
          That happens when someone express their thoughts and feelings without regard
          for others. Aggressive communication appears dominating and controlling,
          frequently interrupting others, invading personal space, and belittling
          others to get their point across. This lead to conflict and resentment."
      - responseText: One of them has been unhappy with the activities planned for
          the opening from the start but says nothing about their feelings in fear
          of appearing a "party-pooper"
        responseFeedback: "They is being a bit passive or submissive, don\u2019t
          you think? That happens when someone avoids expressing their thoughts or
          feelings, often out of fear of conflict"
      - responseText: One of them states the opening has to be postponed for another
          day explaining the reasons behind this change.
        responseFeedback: The assertive style of communication is characterized by
          clear, direct messages. This allows you to express your thoughts and needs
          in a respectful way.
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: Thanks for your opinion!
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    requiresAllFeedback: 1
    isBranchingConflict: 0
  - dialogues:
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: "Tell me\u2026 Have you ever had a friend like this?"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: "Yes, I have (or had) a friend who always criticizes the way
          the other friends either dress when they go out (\"you are so out of fashion\")
          or criticizes their gaming skills\u2026 but is unwilling to explain why
          or open to dialogue."
        responseFeedback: 
      - responseText: "Yes,  I have a friend who never says no. A friend who never
          complains even if they is unhappy with the situation\u2026"
        responseFeedback: 
    requiresAllFeedback: 0
    isBranchingConflict: 1
  - dialogues:
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: "Now, listen carefully\u2026 find your inner silence to be able to go
        beyond words\u2026 What do you think is really happening?"
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: "Someone who is always criticizing the decisions you make\u2026"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: "Maybe is afraid of something\u2026 "
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
      - responseText: "Maybe just doesn\u2019t like us..."
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
      - responseText: Maybe is been hurt in the past and is still angry
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: How can you respond to them?
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: "To the one who is always criticizing the decisions you make\u2026"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: I think you should be less abrasive to people, it is not nice!
        responseFeedback: Well, your message is clear but perhaps not very compassionate
          with this person.
      - responseText: Well, from now on I will criticize everything you say!
        responseFeedback: Maybe you are acting too impulsively, your behavior is
          the same you criticize!
      - responseText: 'I have the impression that something is eating you up. Do
          you wanna talk about it? '
        responseFeedback: "Great, you are being clear but compassionate. To be respectful,
          always think about how you would want to be told\u2026 "
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: What you have just practiced is what we call the ABC of good communication.
        No matter what stage of a relationship you are in, it is important to communicate
        in the right way so that everyone feels safe...
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    requiresAllFeedback: 0
    isBranchingConflict: 0
  - dialogues:
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: "Now, listen carefully\u2026 find your inner silence to be able to go
        beyond words\u2026 What do you think is really happening?"
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: "The one who is unhappy but says nothing\u2026"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: Maybe is afraid of being rejected by the other friends
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
      - responseText: Maybe needs to be asked to be able to express themself
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
      - responseText: "Maybe doesn\u2019t think their friends will appreciate their
          thoughts"
        responseFeedback: "very well, yes... we can't be sure, but that may be it\u2026
          To be a good listener you have to pay attention not only to the words,
          but the underlying meaning of them, try to understand what is really important
          for this person."
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: How can you respond to them?
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    - characterName: Wise Man
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8c68f6b9ce088b641a9b60416829e8d6, type: 3}
      text: "To the one who is unhappy with the planned activity but says nothing\u2026"
      requiresResponse: 1
      responseOptions:
      - responseText: "You never say what\u2019s on your mind, what you really think.
          It is very difficult to be your friend!"
        responseFeedback: Well, your message is clear but perhaps not very compassionate
          with this person.
      - responseText: "You are a dear friend of us, please do not think that we don\u2019t
          want to hear your opinions. Your opinions are important and we want to
          know them"
        responseFeedback: "Great, you are being clear but compassionate. To be respectful,
          always think about how you would want to be told\u2026"
      - responseText: "Sometimes I think you don\u2019t have a mind of your own.
          Do you ever have an opinion on something?"
        responseFeedback: Well, your message is clear but perhaps not very compassionate
          with this person.
    - characterName: Wise Woman
      portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fb8cbc286be4a5429407a23e048c481, type: 3}
      text: What you have just practiced is what we call the ABC of good communication.
        No matter what stage of a relationship you are in, it is important to communicate
        in the right way so that everyone feels safe...
      requiresResponse: 0
      responseOptions: []
    requiresAllFeedback: 0
    isBranchingConflict: 0
  conflict1Concepts:
  - term: Respectful
    description: That means trying to understand and showing interest in the experience
      and perspective of others, although you disagree.
  - term: Real
    description: That means being authentic and sincere, not fake. Expressing your
      true beliefs, even if they may be challenging, disappointing, or uncomfortable
      for others.
  - term: Responsible
    description: That means being accountable for your actions and feelings. Not
      blaming others for your problems.
  - term: Responsive
    description: That means avoiding impulsive reactions. Responding with compassion
      and understanding.
  conflict3Concepts:
  - term: Active listening
    description: is the practice of giving your full attention to the person who
      is talking to you, practicing non-judgment. To be a good listener you have
      to make an inner silence to allow the other person message to be clearly received.
      Be careful when the other person talks to you, go beyond the words and do your
      best to look for meaning. What is important for this person?
  - term: Brief messages
    description: "Keep your message as brief as possible, but complete. A good communicator
      tries to get his or her point across effectively, with detail but without unnecessary
      detail. To be clear, think about what is really important in what you want
      to say and say it as concisely as possible.\r"
  - term: Compassion
    description: Empathetic communication is characterized by understanding and sharing
      the feelings of others. This people-oriented communication prioritizes building
      and nurturing relationships. To be respectful, think about how you would like
      people to be addressed.
